# PathFuse relay — allow management-overlay control ports + data ports.
# Loaded as a drop-in; install.sh MERGES these into the existing inet filter input
# chain (it does not flush the ruleset).
#
# Note these APPEND, so re-running the drop-in duplicates them. Harmless (they are
# all `accept`), but prune before re-applying if you care about a tidy chain.

# SSH over the management overlay, exempt from any rate limit on port 22.
# `insert` (head of chain), NOT `add`: a hardened relay typically carries
# something like `tcp dport 22 ct state new limit rate 10/minute accept`, and an
# APPENDED accept sits after it — so once the limit trips, new SYNs fall through
# to the chain's drop policy and the exemption never applies. Silent hang, not a
# refusal, and retrying only sustains it. Public port 22 keeps its rate limit;
# this exempts the trusted overlay only.
insert rule inet filter input iifname "$overlay_iface" tcp dport 22 accept

add rule inet filter input iifname "$overlay_iface" tcp dport $ports_sbfd_state accept
add rule inet filter input iifname "$overlay_iface" tcp dport $ports_fec_http accept
add rule inet filter input udp dport $ports_engarde accept
